---
title: "withdraw_as_coin (Pebble Protocol: Lending Entry Points)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_validate: validate_market(market)
    q_validate --> q_version: ensure_version_matches()
    q_version --> q_circuit_break: check circuit_break
    q_circuit_break --> q_error_cb: circuit_break triggered
    q_error_cb --> [*]: abort market_under_circuit_break
    q_circuit_break --> q_timestamp: now = clock.timestamp_ms() / 1000
    q_timestamp --> q_handle_withdraw: handle_withdraw(obligation_id, ctoken_to_burn, registry, oracle, clock, now, ctx)
    q_handle_withdraw --> q_update_reward: update_obligation_reward_manager(deposit_reward_type, ctokens_remaining)
    q_update_reward --> q_emit: emit WithdrawEvent
    q_emit --> [*]: return (coin, ctokens_remaining)

    note right of q_handle_withdraw
        INV-001: ctoken_amount must be non-zero
        INV-002: withdraw must not be paused for this asset
        INV-003: obligation must belong to this market
        INV-004: obligation must remain safe after withdrawal
        INV-005: deposit rate limiter outflow is added
        INV-006: reserve cash >= cash_reserve after underlying withdrawal
        INV-007: all obligation interest refreshed before safety check
    end note
